 "script": {
  "hook": "One message, three buzzes. How do you stop duplicate notifications?",
  "question": "Design notification dedupe and badge counts.",
  "trap": "The trap: show every push as it arrives. Retries and extra devices create duplicates, and the badge drifts.",
  "steps": [
   "Stable id. Every message carries one id, so a retry is the same notification.",
   "Collapse key. Show one notification per chat, and replace the old one.",
   "Seen set. The device stores handled ids. A repeat push is dropped.",
   "Badge from truth. Set the badge to the server unread total, never add one."
  ],
  "takeaway": "Same id, one notification. The server sets the badge.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: a new series. Analytics. Event schema and naming.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
